Bing's seam with the end clause imposed (COMMISSION.md sec. 2.3); consolidations of at most 9 blocks.
H is a width-two consolidation of the inner chain D(h+1, k-1) with respect to E(2, m-1),
satisfying Bing's end clause at both extremes of the inner chain; the end links of D(h, k),
which meet e_1 or e_m, are attached to their neighbours' blocks at the regroup.

